        "text": "Tim, what are you building? I'm building Twizen, which is a platform that allows users to create their own trivia games. On Solana, you would create a game with questions. You give back a game code and share it with your friends. Your friends take the game code and they join the game and compete with each other at the same time. And there's an entrance fee, and the winners take the pop. Awesome. So it's like basically pay to learn, Kind of. Yeah. One thing that we think will be awesome is for Web3 companies to use it to incentivize their users to learn about their products. So Jupiter or Solana foundation, someone could sponsor a game and pay the fee, put in their own tokens in the pool, and then say, hey, we're having a trivia game about a white paper or upcoming dao vote. So people will go study and learn the material and then take the trivia game and compete against other people. Cool. How can people get started? If you go to twizzen.com we have our telegram and our X account and you can follow our progress. We're building it right now and soon going to deploy it to Devnet.",
